{"id":12387503,"name":"reachy-mini","ecosystem":"pypi","description":null,"homepage":null,"licenses":null,"normalized_licenses":[],"repository_url":null,"keywords_array":[],"namespace":null,"versions_count":72,"first_release_published_at":"2025-10-15T13:29:46.000Z","latest_release_published_at":"2026-09-21T12:04:49.000Z","latest_release_number":"1.11.0","last_synced_at":"2026-09-26T10:16:08.323Z","created_at":"2025-10-15T13:47:27.018Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T19:15:51.204Z","registry_url":"https://pypi.org/project/reachy-mini/","install_command":"pip install reachy-mini --index-url https://pypi.org/simple","documentation_url":"https://reachy-mini.readthedocs.io/","metadata":{"funding":null,"documentation":null,"classifiers":[],"normalized_name":"reachy-mini","project_status":null},"repo_metadata":{},"repo_metadata_updated_at":null,"dependent_packages_count":0,"downloads":12028,"downloads_period":"last-month","dependent_repos_count":0,"rankings":{"downloads":null,"dependent_repos_count":47.729043041754345,"dependent_packages_count":8.443773090924827,"stargazers_count":null,"forks_count":null,"docker_downloads_count":null,"average":28.086408066339587},"purl":"pkg:pypi/reachy-mini","advisories":[{"uuid":"GSA_kwCzR0hTQS1tMnBjLTNxNHEtdzZqcs4ABlWT","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-m2pc-3q4q-w6jr","title":"reachy_mini Allows Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type","description":"## Summary\n\nThe Reachy Mini daemon exposes the “/api/media/sounds/upload” endpoint without authentication and file validation mechanisms.  \nAn attacker can use this endpoint to upload malicious files into the file system that will propagate in future attacks.\n\n## Compromise Chain: Unauthenticated to Full Root Access\n\nThis issue is part of a full compromise chain allowing an unauthenticated user to gain root access on the Reachy’s operating system:\n\n1. Unrestricted File Upload in Media Sounds Upload API \\\u003c= current finding  \n2. Bluetooth Authentication Bypass  \n3. Bluetooth Directory Traversal\n\n\n## Description\n\nThe root cause of the issue is at the handler located in “***src/daemon/app/routers/media.py***” file at the “upload\\_sound” method:\n\n```py\n@router.post(\"/sounds/upload\")\nasync def upload_sound(\n    file: UploadFile = File(...),\n) -\u003e dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Upload a sound file to the daemon's temporary sound directory.\n    The file is saved to ``/tmp/reachy_mini_sounds/\u003coriginal_filename\u003e``.\n    If a file with the same name already exists it is overwritten.\n    Returns:\n        JSON with the absolute *path* of the saved file on the daemon.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not file.filename:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Filename is required\")\n    # Reject path traversal\n    filename = Path(file.filename).name\n    if not filename or filename in (\".\", \"..\"):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Invalid filename\")\n    os.makedirs(SOUNDS_TMP_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    dest = os.path.join(SOUNDS_TMP_DIR, filename)\n    content = await file.read()\n    with open(dest, \"wb\") as f:\n        f.write(content)\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"path\": dest}\n```\n\nThis endpoint lacks multiple defence mechanisms:\n\n1. No authentication mechanism.  \n2. No file extension validation.  \n3. No file content/size validation.\n\nAdditionally, the daemon is bound to the 0.0.0.0 network interfaces (a.k.a. all network interfaces) by default along with permissive CORS ( allow\\_origins=\\[“\\*”\\] ) meaning the following API endpoint is exposed to every network interface the daemon is connected to.\n\n# PoC\n\n1. Start the daemon in simulation mode (command depends on the installed environment):\n\n```shell\n .venv/bin/mjpython -m reachy_mini.daemon.app.main --sim --no-media\n```\n\n2. After that check that the media upload API endpoint is activated and you can upload a wav file:\n\n```shell\ncurl -X POST http://\u003cdaemon_domain\u003e:\u003cdaemon_port\u003e/api/media/sounds/upload \\\n    -F \"file=@/path/to/your/file.wav\"\n```\n\n3. Now attempt to create a “.sh” file containing a script and upload it:\n\n```shell\ncurl -X POST http://\u003cdaemon_domain\u003e:\u003cdaemon_port\u003e/api/media/sounds/upload \\\n    -F \"file=@/path/to/your/script.sh\"\n```\n\n4. Now error message will be received and you will see that the script file was successfully uploaded to disk.\n\n# Impact\n\nDue to this issue, an attacker can upload malicious files instead of the intended sounds files, harming the integrity of the stored data and allowing an attacker to propagate a foothold in cases another vulnerabilities would arise.\n\n## Fix suggestion\n\nPerform the following check on the API endpoint:\n\n1. Validate that the file extension contains only desired extensions (allow-list approach).  \n2. Validate that the uploaded file’s content matches the desired extension (Magic numbers, and known file structure per file type).  \n3. Enforce authentication on the file upload endpoint.\n\n## Credit\n\nThe vulnerability was discovered by Natan Nehorai of the JFrog Vulnerability Research team.","origin":"UNSPECIFIED","severity":"MODERATE","published_at":"2026-08-25T17:38:43.000Z","withdrawn_at":null,"classification":"GENERAL","cvss_score":5.3,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","references":["https://github.com/pollen-robotics/reachy_mini/security/advisories/GHSA-m2pc-3q4q-w6jr","https://github.com/pollen-robotics/reachy_mini/commit/984c7723b3ec5da63f4e0a2bcf9f120ceb563e04","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-m2pc-3q4q-w6jr"],"source_kind":"github","identifiers":["GHSA-m2pc-3q4q-w6jr","CVE-2026-55419"],"repository_url":null,"blast_radius":0.0,"created_at":"2026-08-25T18:01:30.155Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T17:00:43.300Z","epss_percentage":0.00476,"epss_percentile":0.38516,"api_url":"https://advisories.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/advisories/GSA_kwCzR0hTQS1tMnBjLTNxNHEtdzZqcs4ABlWT","html_url":"https://advisories.ecosyste.ms/advisories/GSA_kwCzR0hTQS1tMnBjLTNxNHEtdzZqcs4ABlWT","packages":[{"ecosystem":"pypi","package_name":"reachy-mini","versions":[{"first_patched_version":"1.8.2","vulnerable_version_range":"\u003c 1.8.2"}],"purl":"pkg:pypi/reachy-mini"}],"related_packages_url":"https://advisories.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/advisories/GSA_kwCzR0hTQS1tMnBjLTNxNHEtdzZqcs4ABlWT/related_packages","related_advisories":[]}],"docker_usage_url":"https://docker.ecosyste.ms/usage/pypi/reachy-mini","docker_dependents_count":null,"docker_downloads_count":null,"usage_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/usage/pypi/reachy-mini","dependent_repositories_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/usage/pypi/reachy-mini/dependencies","status":null,"funding_links":[],"critical":null,"issue_metadata":null,"versions_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/versions","version_numbers_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/version_numbers","latest_version_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/latest_version","dependent_packages_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/dependent_packages","related_packages_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/related_packages","codemeta_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/packages/reachy-mini/codemeta","maintainers":[{"uuid":"pollen-robotics","login":"pollen-robotics","name":null,"email":null,"url":null,"packages_count":19,"html_url":"https://pypi.org/user/pollen-robotics/","role":"Owner","created_at":"2025-10-15T20:55:33.655Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T20:55:33.655Z","packages_url":"https://packages.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/registries/pypi.org/maintainers/pollen-robotics/packages"}]}